  "evidence": "color.expired is text only on paper, paper-inset and background, and a surface, graphic fill or cursor background elsewhere. Measured with just contrast: expired on paper 4.62:1, on paper-inset 4.54:1, on paper-deep 4.43:1, so expired text on paper-deep fails WCAG 2.1 1.4.3 and is listed under disallowed. On the source website it is a surface (background with paper text), a graphic fill (on the sprout-fill track) and a cursor background (expired freshness state). No text, border or stroke uses it, and chips on paper-deep never contain expired content. extension.destructive on extension.card covers expired-coloured text in extensions.",
